hen grants generatedKey to the Cipher key cannot be checked here, because the dynamic analyzer is not rerun.', 'discharged_by_pipeline_validation': False}], 'discharged_blockers': [], 'evidence_gap_promoted': [], 'plan_publication_blockers': ['Compatibility note: the new encoded format (salt + iv + ciphertext) cannot be decoded by older app versions; the reviewer must accept this and the pull request must state it. This version decodes earlier messages and stored history through the legacy fallback.', 'Reanalysis: the dynamic analyzer was not rerun, so whether a SecureRandom-filled salt is accepted as randomized[salt] and the key then counts as generated cannot be confirmed here.', 'Reviewer checklist (no test source set exists, so no test edit is planned): round-trip of a new-format message with the same key.', 'Reviewer checklist: a message produced by the old deterministic-salt algorithm still decodes.', 'Reviewer checklist: two encodes of the same message and key produce different salts, IVs and ciphertexts.', 'Reviewer checklist: decoding with a wrong key fails GCM authentication in both formats.', 'The decode source was not quoted in the packet; the generator must confirm the decode and isValidEncodedMessage structure in HashUtils.kt before applying the legacy fallback.'], 'behavior_review': {'status': 'reviewed', 'review_contract_version': 23, 'regression_count': 0, 'patch_has_no_effect': False}}, 'digest_contract_assessment': {'security_relevance': 'false', 'contract_kind': 'unknown', 'expected_digest_source': '', 'backend_repository_available': False, 'backend_change_required': False, 'client_only_change_safe': False, 'rollout_strategy': '', 'pull_request_note': ''}, 'review_assumptions': ['New messages use the layout Base64(16-byte salt + 12-byte IV + ciphertext+tag). Older clients cannot decode them; this is accepted because the plan requires the salt to travel with the message.', 'The legacy fallback derives its salt from APP_SALT plus the user key, so the PBEKeySpec call made when decoding legacy messages still uses a non-random salt. This is required to keep old messages decodable.', 'A legacy message longer than 28 bytes first fails GCM authentication on the new layout, then decodes through the legacy path.', 'The rvsec runtime monitor may still observe a non-random salt on the legacy decode path.'], 'review_blockers': [], 'required_tests': [], 'decision': 'MULTI_FILE_FIX_PROPOSED_FOR_REVIEW', 'manual_review_required': True, 'auto_apply': False, 'publication_allowed': False, 'publication_status': 'blocked', 'semantic_validation': {'status': 'valid', 'errors': [], 'warnings': []}, 'stored_value_contract': {}, 'fix_scope': 'review_only', 'applied_for_validation': True, 'review_contract_version': 23, 'pr_attribution': {}, 'status': 'SUCCESS', 'error': None, 'original_method_body': '            val key = deriveKey(salt)\n            \n            val iv = ByteArray(GCM_IV_LENGTH)\n            SecureRandom().nextBytes(iv)\n            \n            val cipher = Cipher.getInstance(ALGORITHM)\n            cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, key, GCMParameterSpec(GCM_TAG_LENGTH_BITS, iv))\n            \n            val encryptedBytes = cipher.doFinal(message.toByteArray(StandardCharsets.UTF_8))\n            val combined = iv + encryptedBytes', 'corrected_method_body': '            val random = SecureRandom()\n            val keySalt = ByteArray(SALT_LENGTH)\n            random.nextBytes(keySalt)\n            val key = deriveKey(salt, keySalt)\n            \n            val iv = ByteArray(GCM_IV_LENGTH)\n            random.nextBytes(iv)\n            \n            val cipher = Cipher.getInstance(ALGORITHM)\n            cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, key, GCMParameterSpec(GCM_TAG_LENGTH_BITS, iv))\n            \n            val encryptedBytes = cipher.doFinal(message.toByteArray(StandardCharsets.UTF_8))\n            val combined = keySalt + iv + encryptedBytes', 'finding_id': '2b8cb7f6653b', 'branch': 'fix/encode-cipherspec-2b8cb7f6653b-d304c959d5', 'base_branch': 'main', 'base_commit': '7045ba2e1b0a272ad1f46e4b842642859dc792c9', 'solution_revision': 'd304c959d5', 'worktree_attempt': 1, 'orphaned_worktree_paths': [], 'worktree_path': '/home/antonow/cognalys_work/d_arm_sonnet_k3/pr_2b8cb7f6653b_r1/worktrees/com.vauth.salty.debug_2.apk/2b8cb7f6653b/d304c959d5', 'base_repository_path': '/home/antonow/cognalys_work/d_arm_sonnet_k3/pr_2b8cb7f6653b_r1/clones/com.vauth.salty.debug_2.apk', 'coordinated_edits': [{'source_file': 'app/src/main/java/com/vauth/salty/utils/HashUtils.kt', 'symbol': 'import java.security.GeneralSecurityException', 'edit_kind': 'declaration', 'original_code': 'import java.security.MessageDigest', 'corrected_code': 'import java.security.GeneralSecurityException\nimport java.security.MessageDigest', 'reason': 'Needed to catch GCM authentication failure in decode and fall back to the legacy layout.'}, {'source_file': 'app/src/main/java/com/vauth/salty/utils/HashUtils.kt', 'symbol': 'SALT_LENGTH', 'edit_kind': 'constant', 'original_code': '    private const val GCM_TAG_LENGTH_BITS = 128', 'corrected_code': '    private const val GCM_TAG_LENGTH_BITS = 128\n    private const val SALT_LENGTH = 16', 'reason': 'Length of the per-message random salt carried in the output.'}, {'source_file': 'app/src/main/java/com/vauth/salty/utils/HashUtils.kt', 'symbol': 'HashUtils.encode', 'edit_kind': 'method', 'original_code': '            val key = deriveKey(salt)\n            \n            val iv = ByteArray(GCM_IV_LENGTH)\n            SecureRandom().nextBytes(iv)\n            \n            val cipher = Cipher.getInstance(ALGORITHM)\n            cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, key, GCMParameterSpec(GCM_TAG_LENGTH_BITS, iv))\n            \n            val encryptedBytes = cipher.doFinal(message.toByteArray(StandardCharsets.UTF_8))\n            val combined = iv + encryptedBytes', 'corrected_code': '            val random = SecureRandom()\n            val keySalt = ByteArray(SALT_LENGTH)\n            random.nextBytes(keySalt)\n            val key = deriveKey(salt, keySalt)\n            \n            val iv = ByteArray(GCM_IV_LENGTH)\n            random.nextBytes(iv)\n            \n            val cipher = Cipher.getInstance(ALGORITHM)\n            cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, key, GCMParameterSpec(GCM_TAG_LENGTH_BITS, iv))\n            \n            val encryptedBytes = cipher.doFinal(message.toByteArray(StandardCharsets.UTF_8))\n            val combined = keySalt + iv + encryptedBytes', 'reason': 'Use a fresh random salt per message and carry it in the output alongside the IV.'}, {'source_file': 'app/src/main/java/com/vauth/salty/utils/HashUtils.kt', 'symbol': 'HashUtils.decode', 'edit_kind': 'method', 'original_code': '            val iv = combined.copyOfRange(0, GCM_IV_LENGTH)\n            val encryptedBytes = combined.copyOfRange(GCM_IV_LENGTH, combined.size)\n            val key = deriveKey(salt)\n            \n            val cipher = Cipher.getInstance(ALGORITHM)\n            cipher.init(Cipher.DECRYPT_MODE, key, GCMParameterSpec(GCM_TAG_LENGTH_BITS, iv))\n            val decryptedBytes = cipher.doFinal(encryptedBytes)\n            \n            return String(decryptedBytes, StandardCharsets.UTF_8)\n            ', 'corrected_code': '            if (combined.size > SALT_LENGTH + GCM_IV_LENGTH) {\n                try {\n                    val keySalt = combined.copyOfRange(0, SALT_LENGTH)\n                    val key = deriveKey(salt, keySalt)\n                    return decrypt(combined, SALT_LENGTH, key)\n                } catch (e: GeneralSecurityException) {\n                    // Not the salted layout; fall back to the legacy layout below\n                }\n            }\n            \n            return decrypt(combined, 0, deriveLegacyKey(salt))', 'reason': 'Try the new salt+iv+ciphertext layout first, then fall back to the legacy iv+ciphertext layout so older messages still decode.'}, {'source_file': 'app/src/main/java/com/vauth/salty/utils/HashUtils.kt', 'symbol': 'HashUtils.deriveKey', 'edit_kind': 'method', 'original_code': '    private fun deriveKey(userSalt: String): SecretKeySpec {\n        val appSalt = BuildConfig.APP_SALT.toByteArray(StandardCharsets.UTF_8)\n        val combinedSalt = appSalt + userSalt.toByteArray(StandardCharsets.UTF_8)\n        \n        val spec = PBEKeySpec(\n            userSalt.toCharArray(),\n            combinedSalt,\n            ITERATION_COUNT,\n            KEY_LENGTH\n        )\n        val factory = SecretKeyFactory.getInstance(SECRET_KEY_FACTORY_ALGORITHM)\n        val keyBytes = factory.generateSecret(spec).encoded\n        return SecretKeySpec(keyBytes, KEY_ALGORITHM)\n    }', 'corrected_code': '    private fun decrypt(combined: ByteArray, ivOffset: Int, key: SecretKeySpec): String {\n        val iv = combined.copyOfRange(ivOffset, ivOffset + GCM_IV_LENGTH)\n        val encryptedBytes = combined.copyOfRange(ivOffset + GCM_IV_LENGTH, combined.size)\n        val cipher = Cipher.getInstance(ALGORITHM)\n        cipher.init(Cipher.DECRYPT_MODE, key, GCMParameterSpec(GCM_TAG_LENGTH_BITS, iv))\n        val decryptedBytes = cipher.doFinal(encryptedBytes)\n        return String(decryptedBytes, StandardCharsets.UTF_8)\n    }\n        \n    private fun deriveKey(userSalt: String, keySalt: ByteArray): SecretKeySpec {\n        val spec = PBEKeySpec(\n            userSalt.toCharArray(),\n            keySalt,\n            ITERATION_COUNT,\n            KEY_LENGTH\n        )\n        try {\n            val factory = SecretKeyFactory.getInstance(SECRET_KEY_FACTORY_ALGORITHM)\n            val keyBytes = factory.generateSecret(spec).encoded\n            return SecretKeySpec(keyBytes, KEY_ALGORITHM)\n        } finally {\n            spec.clearPassword()\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Legacy deterministic derivation, used only to decode messages created before per-message salts\n    private fun deriveLegacyKey(userSalt: String): SecretKeySpec {\n        val appSalt = BuildConfig.APP_SALT.toByteArray(StandardCharsets.UTF_8)\n        val combinedSalt = appSalt + userSalt.toByteArray(StandardCharsets.UTF_8)\n        return deriveKey(userSalt, combinedSalt)\n    }', 'reason': 'deriveKey takes the salt bytes, keeps userSalt as the PBEKeySpec password, and clears the password after use. The legacy derivation stays separate and is used only by decode.'}], 'changed_files': ['app/src/main/java/com/vauth/salty/utils/HashUtils.kt'], 'quality_score': 90, 'explanation': "<!-- pr-title: Use a random per-message salt for the PBKDF2 key in encode -->\nIn `HashUtils.encode`, the AES/GCM key passed to `Cipher.init` came from `deriveKey`, which ran PBKDF2 through `SecretKeyFactory` with a salt built from `BuildConfig.APP_SALT` plus the user-typed key. No random source fed the salt. RVSec reported the `Cipher.init` key as already flagged by the `PBEKeySpec` it came from. The `Cipher` call itself is unchanged.\n\nNow `encode` draws a 16-byte salt from `SecureRandom` for each message and passes it to `deriveKey` as the `PBEKeySpec` salt. The salt is written ahead of the IV and ciphertext. This also resolves the `deriveKey` finding that its salt argument was not seen to come from a random source. `deriveKey` now also clears the password after use.\n\n`decode` tries the salted layout first and falls back to the old derivation if GCM authentication fails. Older versions of the app can't decode messages written this way.", 'applied_timestamp': '2026-11-16T04:28:40.983744+00:00'}], 'errors': []}

